meta {
  name: Communities - Delete
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

delete {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "<the name of the community>"
  }
}

docs {
  The owner deletes the community, for good (ADR 0035): its spaces, the content of every member and the files go at once. `name` is the name of the community that you delete, whatever the case: the request names the community, as the screen asks.

  Token ability: `communities:delete`, never in the default set of a new token (the token screen shows it as its own choice). `communities:write` does not delete a community.

  Answers 204. Errors: 400 for a missing `name` or a name that is not the name of the community (the field is named in `errors`), 401 without a token, 403 without the ability and for anyone but the owner, 404 for a community that does not exist.
}
